    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d25">

                <pb facs="0125" n="23" xml:id="pg23"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/5795</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Far Eastern
                        Affairs (Hornbeck) of a Conversation With the Chinese Chargé
                    (Kung)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-01-07">January 7, 1933</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. Kung telephoned me this morning and stated that he has received a cable from
                    the Nanking Government stating that rumors which have appeared in the press to
                    the effect that China is considering the possibility of withdrawing from the
                    League of Nations and the possibility of breaking off diplomatic relations with
                    Japan are altogether unfounded.</p>
                <closer><signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">tanley</hi>] K. H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ornbeck</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
